---
title: "Chemistry"
---

## CHM 05 - Developmental Chemistry for Health Sciences
**Credits**: 1-5

***Prerequisite***: MDE 10

Introduces basic principles of inorganic, organic, and biological chemistry. Emphasizes applications to the health sciences.

## CHM 101 - Introductory Chemistry
**Credits**: 4

***Prerequisite***: Competency level MDE 54 (MTE 1-5).

Explores the experimental and theoretical concepts of general chemistry while emphasizing scientific reasoning, critical and analytical thinking. Designed for the non-science major. This is a Passport Transfer course. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 6 hours per week.

## CHM 111 - General Chemistry I
**Credits**: 4

***Prerequisites***: MDE 61 and EDE 11 Eligible

Explores the fundamental laws, theories, and mathematical concepts of chemistry. Designed primarily for science and engineering majors. Requires a strong background in mathematics. Students must earn a grade of C or higher in the lecture portion of the course to earn an overall grade of C or higher. Part I of II. This is a Passport Transfer course. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 6 hours per week.

## CHM 112 - General Chemistry II
**Credits**: 4

***Prerequisite***: CHM 111 with a grade of C or higher

Explores the fundamental laws, theories, and mathematical concepts of chemistry. Designed primarily for science and engineering majors. Requires a strong background in mathematics. Students must earn a grade of C or higher in the lecture portion of the course to earn an overall grade of C or higher. Part II of II. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 6 hours per week.

## CHM 241 - Organic Chemistry I
**Credits**: 3

***Prerequisites***: CHM 112 with a grade of C or higher

Introduces fundamental chemistry of carbon compounds, including structures, physical properties, syntheses, and typical reactions. Emphasizes reaction mechanisms. Part I of II

Lecture 3 hours. Total 3 hours per week.

## CHM 242 - Organic Chemistry II
**Credits**: 3

***Prerequisite***: CHM 241 with grade of C or higher

Introduces fundamental chemistry of carbon compounds, including structures, physical properties, syntheses, and typical reactions. Emphasizes reaction mechanisms. Part II of II. Lecture 3 hours. Total 3 hours per week.

## CHM 245 - Organic Chemistry I Laboratory
**Credits**: 2

***Prerequisite***: CHM 112 with a grade of C or better

***Corequisite***: CHM 241

Introduces various methods and procedures used in present day organic laboratories. Covers the general techniques, organic synthesis, and the use of common spectroscopic instrumentation; synthesizing a variety of compounds; and analyzing the products through physical properties and spectroscopy. Part I of II. Lecture 1 hour. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 4 hours per week.

## CHM 246 - Organic Chemistry II Laboratory
**Credits**: 2

***Prerequisite***: CHM 245

***Corequisite***: CHM 242

Introduces various methods and procedures used in present day organic laboratories. Covers the general techniques, organic synthesis, and the use of common spectroscopic instrumentation; synthesizing a variety of compounds; and analyzing the products through physical properties and spectroscopy. Part II of II. Lecture 1 hour. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 4 hours per week.

## CHM 299 - Supervised Study
**Credits**: 1

Assigns problems for independent study incorporating previous instruction and supervised by the instructor.

May be repeated for credit. Variable hours.
